# Docker Secrets Reference
# ========================
# This file documents all required secret files for the MMPP stack.
# 
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Create the ./secrets/ directory: mkdir -p secrets
# 2. Create each secret file with the appropriate value: echo "your-secret" > secrets/secret_name.txt
# 3. Set restrictive permissions: chmod 600 secrets/*.txt
# 4. NEVER commit actual secret values to version control
#
# FOR PRODUCTION:
# - Replace these files with values from your secret vault (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, etc.)
# - Use Docker Swarm secrets or Kubernetes secrets for orchestration
# - Consider using tools like docker-secret-env or external-secrets-operator

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED SECRETS
# ============================================================================

# PostgreSQL superuser password (used by initdb and Kestra)
# File: secrets/kestra_postgres_password.txt
# Used by: postgres service (POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE), kestra service (KESTRA_CONFIGURATION)
# Example: k3str4

# FinPay application database password
# File: secrets/finpay_db_password.txt
# Used by: postgres service (FINPAY_DB_PASSWORD_FILE)
# Example: finpay

# FinPay Transaction database password
# File: secrets/finpay_txn_db_password.txt
# Used by: postgres service (FINPAY_TXN_DB_PASSWORD_FILE)
# Example: finpay_txn

# Superset metadata database password
# File: secrets/superset_db_password.txt
# Used by: postgres service (SUPERSET_DB_PASSWORD_FILE), superset service, superset-mcp service
# Example: superset

# LinkAja application database password
# File: secrets/linkaja_db_password.txt
# Used by: postgres service (LINKAJA_DB_PASSWORD_FILE)
# Example: linkaja

# Kestra basic auth password (for Kestra UI access)
# File: secrets/kestra_basic_auth_password.txt
# Used by: kestra service (basic-auth password)
# Example: Admin1234!

# Superset secret key (Flask session signing, CSRF, etc.)
# File: secrets/superset_secret_key.txt
# Used by: superset service, superset-mcp service (SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY_FILE)
# CRITICAL: Must be a long, random string (min 32 chars)
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 42
# Example: super-secret-key-for-metadata-db-please-change-in-production

# Superset admin user password (initial bootstrap)
# File: secrets/superset_admin_password.txt
# Used by: superset service (fab create-admin)
# Example: change-me

# ============================================================================
# KESTRA WORKFLOW SECRETS (stored in .env_encoded, not Docker Secrets)
# ============================================================================
# These are base64-encoded secrets for Kestra workflows:
# SECRET_FINPAY_DB_HOST, SECRET_FINPAY_DB_PORT, SECRET_FINPAY_DB_NAME
# SECRET_FINPAY_DB_USER, SECRET_FINPAY_DB_PASSWORD
# SECRET_FINPAY_TOPUP_WEBHOOK_KEY, SECRET_DIGIPOS_PASSWORD
# SECRET_GCP_SA_KEY, SECRET_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, SECRET_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
# SECRET_FINPAY_SPREADSHEET_*, SECRET_FINPAY_PROTECTION_*, SECRET_FINPAY_MANDIRI_*
# Stored in: .env_encoded (base64-encoded values)
# Example: .env_encoded.example

# ============================================================================
# PRODUCTION SECRET ROTATION
# ============================================================================
# 1. Rotate secrets every 90 days (or per compliance requirements)
# 2. Use automated rotation via vault (Vault Agent, AWS Secrets Manager rotation)
# 3. Update secret files atomically (write to temp, mv)
# 4. Signal services to reload (SIGHUP or restart)
# 5. Audit access logs after rotation

# ============================================================================
# VAULT INTEGRATION EXAMPLES
# ============================================================================
# HashiCorp Vault (Docker):
#   vault kv get -field=password secret/mmpp/postgres > secrets/kestra_postgres_password.txt
#
# AWS Secrets Manager:
#   aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id mmpp/postgres --query SecretString --output text > secrets/kestra_postgres_password.txt
#
# Azure Key Vault:
#   az keyvault secret show --vault-name mmpp-vault --name postgres-password --query value -o tsv > secrets/kestra_postgres_password.txt
#
# 1Password CLI:
#   op read "op://MMMP/Postgres/password" > secrets/kestra_postgres_password.txt
